---
import { LINKS } from "../../data/site.js";
import Section from "../Section.astro";
import Cells from "./Cells.astro";
import Head from "./Head.astro";
---

<Section id="limits" cross>
  <Head label="Limitations" title="What it does not do yet" />
  <Cells cols={2}>
    <p class="limit">Rejected real audio is harder to recognize, but no model has yet been trained on the kept audio to show it does better. That run is planned and has not been done.</p>
    <p class="limit">On real phone speech the SNR floor rejected music-bed recordings that recognizers handled well. Check what it removes before relying on it.</p>
    <p class="limit">A single sustained instrument can pass as speech, and babble reads cleaner than it is.</p>
    <p class="limit">Transcripts are per file: <code>curate</code> copies one to every clip cut from that file, with no alignment or speech recognition. For audio already cut per utterance, score it whole with <code>inspect(..., whole=True)</code>.</p>
  </Cells>
  <Cells>
    <div class="foot">
      <p>Speech is found from signal level by default, so loud music counts as speech. Silero VAD is optional and the command-line tool does not expose it yet.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href={`${LINKS.github}#limitations`}>Read the full list<span class="arrow">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </Cells>
</Section>

<style>
  .limit { color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .foot { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 16px 32px; }
  .foot p { color: var(--ink-soft); max-width: 64ch; }
</style>
